STEP 1 — MedicalVault.jsx: Add Biomarker Trend Timeline section. Add props: the component currently receives {archive, loadingArchive, expandedId, setExpandedId}. Since MedicalVault doesn't directly fetch, it needs pathology data. The archive prop already contains pathology records (type='pathology'). Use archive client-side to build trends: filter archive for type='pathology', parse each record's report_data, group by biomarker name.
  Add state inside MedicalVault:
  const [selectedBiomarker, setSelectedBiomarker] = useState(null);
  const [showTrends, setShowTrends] = useState(false);
  Compute trendData from archive:
  const trendData = useMemo(() => { ... group pathology records by biomarker name ... }, [archive]);
  const biomarkerNames = Object.keys(trendData).sort();
  Build trend grouping: for each pathology record in archive where type==='pathology', parse report_data (list of {name, value, unit}), for each biomarker create/append to trendData[normalizedName].data = [{date: record.created_at.split('T')[0], value: parseFloat(b.value), source_id: record.id, unit: b.unit}].
